## Technical Notes
================================================================================

### Model Configuration (Sprint 3)
- config/models.yaml: central configuration file
- YAML priority over environment variables
- Hot reload: llm_manager.reload_config()
- Get enabled models: llm_manager.get_enabled_llm_models()

### Embedding Performance (Sprint 3)
- Before: 1000 texts ~50 seconds (serial)
- After: 1000 texts <10 seconds (concurrent)
- 5x speedup with configurable batch_size
- Small batches (<10): direct asyncio.gather()
- Large batches: chunked processing with 0.1s delays

### Health Check System (Sprint 3)
- GET /api/v1/health: fast basic check (<100ms)
- GET /api/v1/health/full: complete component check
- Startup check: blocks production, warns development
- Component status: healthy/degraded/unhealthy
- Configurable via models.yaml health_check section

### Citation System (Sprint 3)
- CitationInfo: source tracking + highlight positions
- extract_highlights(): jieba tokenization for Chinese
- UI components: badges, highlighting, source list
- Integration pending: chat service + chat page UI

### Document Upload (Sprint 3)
- Supported formats: PDF, DOCX, Markdown
- File size limit: 10MB
- Auto title extraction from metadata or content
- Parser factory: auto-selects parser by extension
- Immediate indexing after upload

### ChromaDB Integration
- Empty metadata: single doc use None, batch use {"_placeholder": "true"}
- NumPy array check: use `is not None` and `len()` explicitly
- Batch operations: batch_size=100

### Jira Data Structure
- JiraIssue fields: summary, description, comments, labels, status, priority
- Pagination: start_at, max_results

### Embedding Model
- Default: bge-large-zh (1024 dims)
- Usage: manager.create_embedding().embed(text)

### RAG Document Indexing
- Chunking: 800 chars, 150 overlap, smart boundary
- Chunk ID: parent_id_chunk_index
- Score: 1.0 / (1.0 + distance)
- Batch: Jira 50/batch, ChromaDB 100/batch

### Web UI Architecture
- FastAPI backend (7860) + Gradio frontend (7861)
- Session: UUID, memory + JSON persistence, TTL 30min, max 100 messages
- Streaming: Server-Sent Events (SSE)
- Events: start, context, token, end, error

### Hybrid Retrieval
- Methods: vector, bm25, hybrid
- Fusion: rrf (k=60), weighted, linear
- BM25: jieba tokenization, stopword filter, pickle persistence

### Reranker
- Model: bge-reranker-large
- Batch: batch_size=4
- Lazy loading, Sigmoid normalization

